## What to deliver

Build and rig the mech up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: an upright torso on two walking legs, with a
long rail-lance projecting forward from the chest. The required interface is a
caller-driven **`weapon_pitch`** joint that aims the rail-lance up and down about
its chest mount, plus the two auto **`leg_left_stride`** and **`leg_right_stride`**
joints that walk the legs in opposite phase. Produce **every** required part and
joint; you may add your own extra parts, joints, or auto-play clips on top, but do
not drop or contradict the required interface. When you are satisfied, stop: the
recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
